  "title": "One-sided additive paths of every length",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Paths of n >= 3 rings of s >= 4 cells, each ring on rule 60 or 102, every middle ring's contacts two apart (k_j in {2, s - 2}), c_1 reading its partners on R_0 and R_1 and each later contact c_i both neighbours on R_(i-1) and its partner on R_i. After mirroring every rule-102 ring, with e the sum of k_j' - 1: every contact binds both its rings at every lag; the last contact binds R_(n-1) at every lag and R_0 exactly when C(T - (n - 1), e) is odd, so the path composes at recurring lags with every contact persistent at every length and ring size (density 2^(-ones in e)) and at every lag never.",
